  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience is individuals who may be exposed to racially charged misinformation, particularly those who hold or are susceptible to anti-Black stereotypes, such as the belief that Black people are inherently violent or criminal. The meme is designed to appeal to or reinforce these prejudiced views by falsely attributing the 1992 Los Angeles riots to 'African American leaders,' thereby promoting racial scapegoating. It likely targets audiences who are already predisposed to racial division, misinformation, or who benefit from or are entertained by narratives that delegitimize Black protest and community anger. The meme’s hateful intent suggests it is crafted to incite racial tension and reinforce harmful stereotypes, making its primary target community those who consume and share such content without critical analysis.",
